1
00:00:00,076 --> 00:00:04,614
Imagine you are holding a book written
fourteen centuries ago.

2
00:00:05,002 --> 00:00:09,673
When that book was written, people knew
neither the microscope nor the telescope.

3
00:00:10,157 --> 00:00:12,579
No one had ever gone down to the bottom of
the oceans.

4
00:00:12,885 --> 00:00:15,058
No one knew what happens inside the stars.

5
00:00:15,108 --> 00:00:23,387
Yet its pages contain verses touching on topics that
today's science has only recently begun to discuss.

6
00:00:23,744 --> 00:00:28,261
And even more intriguing: twenty-nine
surahs begin with letters

7
00:00:28,451 --> 00:00:32,736
whose meaning no scholar has known for
certain for fourteen centuries.

8
00:00:33,083 --> 00:00:37,971
In this video we will uncover seven
secrets of the Holy Quran together.

9
00:00:38,309 --> 00:00:40,921
We will not force any claim.

10
00:00:41,146 --> 00:00:43,117
We will read the verse,

11
00:00:43,167 --> 00:00:47,697
show today's knowledge, and you will draw
the conclusion yourself.

12
00:00:47,931 --> 00:00:51,627
But on one condition: watch until the last
secret.

13
00:00:51,857 --> 00:00:55,500
Because it is a question no one has been
able to answer.

14
00:00:56,161 --> 00:00:58,636
The first secret is in your hands.

15
00:00:58,882 --> 00:00:59,918
Literally.

16
00:01:00,415 --> 00:01:02,192
The pagans of Mecca used to ask:

17
00:01:02,527 --> 00:01:06,254
Who will bring rotten bones that have
turned to dust back to life?

18
00:01:06,620 --> 00:01:11,199
Surah al-Qiyamah answers: Does man think

19
00:01:11,249 --> 00:01:13,823
that We will not be able to gather his
bones?

20
00:01:14,039 --> 00:01:14,977
Yes!

21
00:01:15,027 --> 00:01:23,133
We are able to restore even his fingertips
as they were.

22
00:01:23,183 --> 00:01:26,282
Notice: the verse mentions neither the
heart nor the brain.

23
00:01:26,725 --> 00:01:29,457
It mentions the fingertips.

24
00:01:29,507 --> 00:01:37,853
In 1880 the Scottish doctor Henry Faulds suspected
that fingerprints differ from person to person.

25
00:01:37,903 --> 00:01:42,763
In 1892 Francis Galton proved it:

26
00:01:42,831 --> 00:01:49,412
no two fingerprints in the world are the
same, and they never change in a lifetime.

27
00:01:49,707 --> 00:01:54,727
From 1905 the police began to identify
criminals this way.

28
00:01:54,986 --> 00:01:59,643
So that tiny point that God said He would
restore is the signature of your identity.

29
00:01:59,776 --> 00:02:06,948
Earlier commentators understood this verse as
"We will restore even the smallest bone."

30
00:02:07,253 --> 00:02:12,370
But today, reading this verse, one thing
stands out.

31
00:02:12,692 --> 00:02:14,448
Do you think this is a coincidence?

32
00:02:14,776 --> 00:02:17,199
The second secret lies at the bottom of
the oceans.

33
00:02:17,435 --> 00:02:21,278
In Surah ar-Rahman we read: He released
the two seas to meet.

34
00:02:21,846 --> 00:02:26,411
Between them is a barrier; they do not
transgress each other's limits.

35
00:02:26,646 --> 00:02:32,445
In the Strait of Gibraltar the
Mediterranean Sea meets the Atlantic
Ocean.

36
00:02:32,629 --> 00:02:37,584
Mediterranean water is saltier and
heavier.

37
00:02:37,634 --> 00:02:42,848
It flows out into the ocean below, while
Atlantic water flows in above.

38
00:02:43,106 --> 00:02:49,733
Between the two water masses forms a boundary
that oceanographers call a transition layer.

39
00:02:49,783 --> 00:02:55,901
To be honest: these waters do not stay completely
separate; they slowly mix at the boundary.

40
00:02:56,022 --> 00:03:00,743
But each keeps its own salinity and
temperature over a long distance.

41
00:03:00,793 --> 00:03:05,061
And the verse does not say "they do not mix"; it says
"they do not transgress each other's limits."

42
00:03:05,111 --> 00:03:09,438
This could only be measured in the
twentieth century with special
instruments.

43
00:03:09,666 --> 00:03:14,482
How could a person living in the desert
have known this?

44
00:03:14,750 --> 00:03:18,450
The third secret is hidden in the name of
a surah: an-Nahl, the Bee.

45
00:03:18,792 --> 00:03:24,282
Your Lord inspired the bee: make homes for
yourself in the mountains and in the trees.

46
00:03:24,913 --> 00:03:29,549
Then eat from all the fruits and follow the
ways your Lord has made easy for you.

47
00:03:29,599 --> 00:03:33,064
In Arabic, verbs have masculine and
feminine forms.

48
00:03:33,114 --> 00:03:37,718
In this verse all three commands — make,
eat, follow — are in the feminine form.

49
00:03:37,768 --> 00:03:40,325
Today biology says: the worker bees that
build the hive,

50
00:03:40,375 --> 00:03:46,694
go from flower to flower and collect honey
are all female.

51
00:03:46,818 --> 00:03:52,104
Male bees neither build the hive nor
collect honey.

52
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:53,891
To be honest: linguists will say

53
00:03:53,941 --> 00:03:56,023
that the Arabic word "nahl" can be used in
the feminine anyway.

54
00:03:56,110 --> 00:03:58,764
That is true.

55
00:03:59,071 --> 00:04:03,789
But the verse chose exactly this form, and it
describes precisely the bee that does the work.

56
00:04:03,839 --> 00:04:05,835
Do you think this is a coincidence?

57
00:04:05,885 --> 00:04:07,704
The fourth secret is not science but
history.

58
00:04:08,199 --> 00:04:10,537
And history can be checked with documents.

59
00:04:10,785 --> 00:04:13,516
The year 614 AD.

60
00:04:13,566 --> 00:04:19,213
The Persian army crushes Byzantium and
takes Jerusalem.

61
00:04:19,522 --> 00:04:21,521
By 619 all of Egypt also falls into
Persian hands.

62
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:23,523
Byzantium is on the verge of collapse.

63
00:04:23,759 --> 00:04:28,543
The pagans of Mecca rejoice: the fire-
worshippers have defeated the People of the
Book.

64
00:04:29,033 --> 00:04:31,601
We will defeat you the same way!

65
00:04:31,972 --> 00:04:34,862
Exactly then Surah ar-Rum is revealed: The
Romans have been defeated.

66
00:04:34,912 --> 00:04:39,016
But after this defeat they will be
victorious within a few years.

67
00:04:39,549 --> 00:04:45,497
The Arabic word "bid'", used for "a few
years", means a number from three to nine.

68
00:04:45,885 --> 00:04:50,356
Abu Bakr, sure of this verse, makes a
wager with the pagans.

69
00:04:50,708 --> 00:04:55,172
And in 622 Emperor Heraclius launches a
counter-offensive.

70
00:04:55,519 --> 00:05:00,960
In 627, at the Battle of Nineveh, he
inflicts a heavy defeat on the Persians.

71
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:06,093
Interestingly, Heraclius's campaign passes
through the Caucasus and historical Azerbaijan,

72
00:05:06,143 --> 00:05:08,237
the lands of Atropatene.

73
00:05:08,655 --> 00:05:14,075
A victory no one expected comes true
within the time foretold.

74
00:05:14,708 --> 00:05:18,496
The fifth secret is on display today in a
museum in Cairo.

75
00:05:18,999 --> 00:05:22,281
As Pharaoh was drowning in the sea, God
said to him:

76
00:05:22,799 --> 00:05:30,609
Today We will save your body, so that you
may be a sign for those after you.

77
00:05:30,677 --> 00:05:33,711
Notice: not your soul, but your body.

78
00:05:33,761 --> 00:05:39,083
When the Quran was revealed, the mummies of the
ancient Egyptian pharaohs lay beneath the sands,

79
00:05:39,133 --> 00:05:40,471
in hidden tombs.

80
00:05:40,761 --> 00:05:45,248
No one could see them.

81
00:05:45,584 --> 00:05:50,801
Only at the end of the nineteenth century
did pharaoh mummies begin to be found.

82
00:05:51,245 --> 00:05:56,801
Today they are in a museum in Cairo,
before the eyes of millions of people.

83
00:05:57,123 --> 00:06:05,329
To be honest: it is not known exactly which
pharaoh lived in the time of Prophet Moses.

84
00:06:05,585 --> 00:06:06,970
Scholars name different ones.

85
00:06:07,020 --> 00:06:13,918
But the word of the verse is precise: that body
will be a lesson for later generations.

86
00:06:14,622 --> 00:06:20,364
And today people come from all over the world to look at the dry
bodies of the rulers who said, "I am your lord most high."

87
00:06:20,504 --> 00:06:22,928
The sixth secret is in the depths of the
universe.

88
00:06:22,978 --> 00:06:25,598
One surah of the Quran is named al-Hadid,
meaning Iron.

89
00:06:25,789 --> 00:06:29,820
And there it says: And We sent down iron.

90
00:06:30,180 --> 00:06:32,862
In it is great strength and benefits for
people.

91
00:06:32,998 --> 00:06:33,998
Sent down.

92
00:06:34,312 --> 00:06:36,059
Not "brought out of the earth" — sent
down.

93
00:06:36,109 --> 00:06:39,397
Today astronomy says: iron is not formed
on Earth.

94
00:06:39,447 --> 00:06:44,290
It forms inside stars about eight times
larger than the Sun.

95
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:48,671
When those stars explode, iron scatters into
space and then becomes part of the planets,

96
00:06:48,721 --> 00:06:50,380
including the Earth.

97
00:06:50,658 --> 00:06:54,945
The European Space Agency explains it this
way as well.

98
00:06:55,105 --> 00:06:55,778
To be honest:

99
00:06:55,828 --> 00:07:01,844
the Arabic verb "anzalna" is also used in the Quran
for livestock and also means "We bestowed".

100
00:07:02,063 --> 00:07:04,921
So this is not the only reading of the
verse.

101
00:07:05,212 --> 00:07:06,381
But just think:

102
00:07:06,631 --> 00:07:12,565
the iron in your blood was once in the
heart of a star that died long ago.

103
00:07:12,979 --> 00:07:15,015
And now the last secret.

104
00:07:15,293 --> 00:07:16,601
The greatest secret.

105
00:07:17,148 --> 00:07:18,188
Open the Quran.

106
00:07:18,497 --> 00:07:20,420
The second surah, al-Baqarah.

107
00:07:20,816 --> 00:07:22,987
The first verse: Alif.

108
00:07:23,051 --> 00:07:23,917
Lam.

109
00:07:23,967 --> 00:07:24,967
Mim.

110
00:07:25,227 --> 00:07:26,581
It is not a word.

111
00:07:26,746 --> 00:07:27,969
It is not a sentence.

112
00:07:28,205 --> 00:07:29,850
Just three letters.

113
00:07:30,226 --> 00:07:31,378
Ya Sin.

114
00:07:31,634 --> 00:07:32,636
Ta Ha.

115
00:07:32,987 --> 00:07:33,714
Qaf.

116
00:07:33,764 --> 00:07:34,764
Nun.

117
00:07:35,084 --> 00:07:38,841
Kaf, Ha, Ya, Ayn, Sad.

118
00:07:39,409 --> 00:07:47,586
Of the Quran's one hundred fourteen surahs,
twenty-nine begin with such mysterious letters.

119
00:07:47,824 --> 00:07:53,136
The letters used are fourteen — exactly
half of the Arabic alphabet.

120
00:07:53,547 --> 00:07:57,233
Their combinations are also fourteen.

121
00:07:57,473 --> 00:08:00,818
Scholars have pondered these letters for
fourteen centuries.

122
00:08:01,131 --> 00:08:03,641
One says: they are the initials of the
names of God.

123
00:08:03,943 --> 00:08:06,550
One says: they are the names of the
surahs.

124
00:08:06,856 --> 00:08:09,164
One says: this is a challenge.

125
00:08:09,214 --> 00:08:13,763
The Quran is made of these very letters
you use every day.

126
00:08:14,187 --> 00:08:16,956
If you can, bring something like it!

127
00:08:17,341 --> 00:08:22,251
But the final word of most scholars is this:
their true meaning is known only to God.

128
00:08:22,301 --> 00:08:23,816
And perhaps this is the greatest secret:

129
00:08:24,067 --> 00:08:31,513
to the human who tries to explain everything, the Quran reminds
at its very beginning that there are things you do not know.

130
00:08:31,975 --> 00:08:33,161
Fingerprints.

131
00:08:33,445 --> 00:08:35,060
Seas that do not mix.

132
00:08:35,302 --> 00:08:36,302
The bee.

133
00:08:36,647 --> 00:08:38,565
The return of an empire.

134
00:08:38,915 --> 00:08:40,492
The body of a pharaoh.

135
00:08:40,883 --> 00:08:42,821
Iron from the stars.

136
00:08:43,073 --> 00:08:45,676
And letters whose meaning remains veiled.

137
00:08:46,225 --> 00:08:49,603
Could each of these, on its own, be a
coincidence?

138
00:08:49,933 --> 00:08:50,925
Perhaps.

139
00:08:50,975 --> 00:08:54,687
But the Quran itself calls its reader to
do one thing:

140
00:08:55,161 --> 00:08:57,788
Do they not reflect upon the Quran?

141
00:08:58,204 --> 00:09:02,546
This book asks not for blind belief, but
for thinking.

142
00:09:02,839 --> 00:09:05,182
And that is exactly what this video was
for.

143
00:09:05,502 --> 00:09:08,818
Which of these seven secrets made you
think the most?

144
00:09:09,056 --> 00:09:10,821
Write its number in the comments.

145
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:15,763
And if you know a secret that is not in
this video, write it too.

146
00:09:15,884 --> 00:09:18,198
We will make another video like this.

147
00:09:18,422 --> 00:09:21,995
Don't forget to like the video and
subscribe to the channel.

148
00:09:22,255 --> 00:09:24,450
Peace of God be upon you.

